\pard\fi0\li0\tx285\tx720\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f0\fs22 1\plain \f2\super\lang1033\fs28 ra\plain \f0\fs22 \endash 16\plain \f2\super\lang1033\fs28 ra\plain \f0\fs22  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f2\scaps\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17 Damasus [Hungarus}}\plain \f2\scaps\lang1033\fs22 ]: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f2\scaps\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17 Summa titulorum [Decretalium}}\plain \f2\scaps\lang1033\fs22 ]\plain \f0\fs22 . \plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 \u8250 \'9bIncipit Summa titulorum a magistro Damaso compilata.\u8249 \'8b {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17 Iuri operam daturum prius nosse oportet, quid sit ius. Est autem ius ars boni et equi}}\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22  ... \endash  ... ut ff \lquote Depositi\rquote  l. \lquote Ei\rquote  \u167 \'a7 ult\plain \f0\fs22 . (Dig. 15.1.5). \plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22 \u8250 \'9bDamasus hic Summam finit / Qui carmine vivit\u8249 \'8b\plain \f0\fs22 . Ed. (teilw.): {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[0].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17 Schulte, Literaturgeschichte, 1841}}\plain \f0\fs22 , S. 89\endash 97 [139\endash 147]; Jean Pierre Renard: Trois sommes de p\u233 \'e9nitence de la premi\u232 \'e8re moiti\u233 \'e9 du XIIIe si\u232 \'e8cle. T. 1\endash 2. Louvain-la-Neuve 1989, Bd. 1, S. 38\endash 44; 456\endash 489; Bd. 2, S. 88; 91; 99; 117. Zu Verfasser, Werk und \u220 \'dcberlieferung vgl. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[1].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17 Kuttner, Repertorium, 1937}}\plain \f0\fs22 , S. 393\endash 396 (Hs genannt). Am Rand Glossen (mit Allegationen und Versus et proverbia iuridica, z. B. 1\plain \f2\super\lang1033\fs28 v\plain \f0\fs22  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[2].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17 Walther, Initia, 1969}}\plain \f0\fs22 , Nr. 3357)\plain \f2\i\lang1033\fs22