\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f0\fs22 2\plain \f0\super\fs28 v\plain \f0\fs22 -267\plain \f0\super\fs28 r\plain \f0\fs22  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs22\chcbpat17 Johannes Butzbach}}\plain \f0\scaps\fs22 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\scaps\fs22\chcbpat17 Philosophilogium}}\plain \f0\fs22 . Mit Widmungsbriefen von Johannes Butzbach an Johannes Senegius (2\plain \f0\super\fs28 v\plain \f0\fs22 ; dat. 1505) sowie seine Lehrer Johannes Condanus, Gotfridus de Colonia, Benedictus de Monasterio Eyfaliae et Petrus Wedanus (3\plain \f0\super\fs28 r\plain \f0\fs22 -12\plain \f0\super\fs28 v\plain \f0\fs22 ), Verfasserregister (13\plain \f0\super\fs28 ra\plain \f0\fs22 -15\plain \f0\super\fs28 rb\plain \f0\fs22 ) und Prolog (15\plain \f0\super\fs28 v\plain \f0\fs22 -16\plain \f0\super\fs28 v\plain \f0\fs22 ). Exzerptsammlung in drei Teilen: Teil I (17\plain \f0\super\fs28 r\plain \f0\fs22 -184\plain \f0\super\fs28 v\plain \f0\fs22 ): Griechische Autoren (Prosa); Teil II (185\plain \f0\super\fs28 r\plain \f0\fs22 -258\plain \f0\super\fs28 v\plain \f0\fs22 ): Lateinische Autoren (Dichtung); Teil III (259\plain \f0\super\fs28 r\plain \f0\fs22 -267\plain \f0\super\fs28 r\plain \f0\fs22 ): Gemischte Exzerpte. (2\plain \f0\super\fs28 v\plain \f0\fs22 ) Widmungsbrief 1 (dat. 1505): {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 Quoniam quidem, fili mi amantissime, ad scholam divini servitii}}\plain \f0\i\fs22  ...\plain \f0\fs22  (3\plain \f0\super\fs28 r\plain \f0\fs22 ) Widmungsbrief 2: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 Quando quidem, venerandi patres ac preceptores mei colendissimi, me nuper admodum ignarum ineptum et indignum}}\plain \f0\i\fs22  ... \plain \f0\fs22 (15\plain \f0\super\fs28 v\plain \f0\fs22 ) Prolog: >\plain \f0\i\fs22 Ad bonarum litterarum optimis sententiis refertarum oppido quam studiosos amatores confratres atque discipulos ymmo et filios suos spirituales in Christi amore dilectissimos fratres Joannis Boitzbagii\plain \f0\fs22  \plain \f0\i\fs22 Piemontani omnium minimi in Philosophilogium suum diversis ex gentilium scriptorum dictis contextum prefatio<.\plain \f0\fs22  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[2].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 Si seperaveris preciosum a vili quasi os meum eris, dicit prophetes}}\plain \f0\i\fs22  ...\plain \f0\fs22  (17\plain \f0\super\fs28 r\plain \f0\fs22 ) Text: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[3].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\i\fs22\chcbpat17 Antiquissimum omnium entium Deus est. Ingenitum enim}}\plain \f0\i\fs22  ... - ... ut apes in saltibus omnia libant.\plain \f0\fs22  Zu Werk und \u220 \'dcberlieferung vgl. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[0].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17 VL Dt. Hum.}}\plain \f0\fs22 , Bd. 1, Sp. 342 (Hs. als Unikat genannt); {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[1].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f0\fs22\chcbpat17 Beriger, Odeporicon, 1991}}\plain \f0\fs22 , S. 49 (P.3; Hs. als Unikat genannt). Am Rand sowie im Text Glossen, Nachtr\u228 \'e4ge und Korrekturen von Butzbach. Handwechsel.}

