\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f0\fs22\cf1 2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 ra\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 201\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17\cf1 Marcus Tullius Cicero}}\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 : [{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17\cf1 Opera}}\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 ]\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 , teilweise Fragmente durch Blattverlust (s. o.), teilweise Pseudo-Cicero (Ps.). \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Wunder (s. o.), S. XIVf. (Textvarianten). Zu Werk und \u220 \'dcber\-lieferung vgl. Munk-Olsen, \u201 \'c9tude, Bd. 1, S. 10ff.; 148\endash 150.\plain \f0\fs22\cf1  (2\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 ra\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 9\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 De officiis\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 , Fragment am Ende (1,1\endash 118). (10\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 ra\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 43\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 va\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 De oratore\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 , Fragment im Inneren (1,1\endash 128; 157\endash 193; 2,13\endash 367; 3,1\endash 17; 110\endash 230). In lib. II h\u228 \'e4ufig Fehlstellen von ausgelassenen W\u246 \'f6rtern. (43\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 59\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 De inventione\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 , Fragment im Inneren (1,1\endash 40; 2,29\endash 178). (59\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 -81\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Rhetorica ad Herennium (Ps.)\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 , Sechs-B\u252 \'fccher-Fassung, Fragment im Inneren und am Ende (1,1\endash 3,33; 4,3\endash 69). (81\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 86\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Topica\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 , Fragment am Ende; danach bis zum Zeilenende eine Rasur. (87\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 ra\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 175\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 va\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) [\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Orationes\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ]: (87\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 ra\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 88\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 va\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 In L. Catilinam\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 , Fragment am Anfang (4,2\endash 24). (88\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 va\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 90\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Pro M. Marcello\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 . (90\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 92\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Pro Q. Ligario\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 . (92\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 94\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Pro rege Deiotaro\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 . (94\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 97\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 In P. Vatinium testem\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 . (97\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 99\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 va\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 pridie quam in exilium iret (Ps.)\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 . (99\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 va\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 102\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 va\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 post reditum in senatu (Ps.)\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 . (102\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 va\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 102\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 post \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 reditum in Quirites\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 , am Ende Fragment (1\endash 6)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22\cf1 . \plain \f0\fs22\cf1 (103\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 ra\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 106\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 va\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 De provinciis consularibus\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 , am Anfang (\u167 \'a7 1) Fragment. (106\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 va\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 112\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 De haruspicum responsis\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 . (112\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 117\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Pro L. Cornelio Balbo\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 . (117\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 123\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Pro M. Caelio\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 . (123\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 125\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Pro A. Licinio Archia poeta\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 . (125\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 132\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 In L. Pisonem\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 . (132\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 137\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 ra\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Pro lege Manilia de imperio Cn. Pompei\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 . (137\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 143\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Pro A. Caecina\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 , am Ende Fragment (1\endash 100). (144\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 ra\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 144\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Pro P. Sulla\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 , am Anfang Fragment (81\endash 93). (144\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 153\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 ra\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Pro Cn. Plancio\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 . (153\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 ra\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 160\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Pro T. Annio Milone\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 . (153\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 r\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) auf dem \u228 \'e4u\u223 \'dferen Rand von nur wenig sp\u228 \'e4terer Hand: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22\cf1 P. Clodius senator seditio\-sus\~...\plain \f0\fs22\cf1  Ed.: Albert C. Clark (Hg.): M. Tulli Ciceronis Pro T. Annio Milone ad iudices oratio. Oxford 1895, S. 135f. (160\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 171\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 ra\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 De lege agraria\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 . (171\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 175\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 va\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 In C. Verrem actio secunda\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 , Exzerpte aus lib. 3\endash 4. (175\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) leer. (176\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 ra\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 186\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 ra\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Epistulae ad familiares\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 . Am Anfang Fragment (lib. 14\endash 16). Die Einzel\-paragraphen (176\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 ra\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) 12,29, 21 und 13,78\endash 79 sind m\u246 \'f6glicherweise Nach\-tr\u228 \'e4ge zuvor vergessener Textpartien. Zur abweichenden Brieffolge in lib.15\endash 16 vgl. Wunder (s. o.), S. XV; 131; 134\endash 136. (186\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 ra\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 186\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Epistula ad Octavianum (Ps.)\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 . Titel fehlt. (186\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 189\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) [\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Quintus Tullius Cicero: De petitione consulatus\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ]. Titel fehlt. (189\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 vb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 195\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Cato maior de senectute\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 . (195\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 va\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 \endash 201\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs28\cf1 rb\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22\cf1 Laelius de amicitia\plain \f0\fs22\cf1 .}

